{
  "opportunity_id": "proc_3add3b927d",
  "source": "content_cluster",
  "title": "Meters with flow but no deal: extend, issue, or write off to UAG",
  "task_class": "deal_entry_correction",
  "label_mechanical": "Deal entry and correction in Sitara / Unify / TAGG: resolve deal / meter / unmatched",
  "narrative": {
    "what_happens": "A meter shows recorded volume on days that no deal ticket covers, so the flow cannot be booked against a contract. Logistics writes to the responsible commercial contact listing the meter, the affected days and the candidate deal numbers, and asks for one of a small set of outcomes: an existing deal extended, a new deal (sometimes with an associated purchase contract) issued, or approval to write the volume off to Unaccounted for Gas. The recipient replies with a deal number or a decision, and the volume is then recorded or written off. The messages follow a near-identical template \u2014 \"Logistics needs either (1) ... (2) new deal, or (3) approval to write-off these volumes to Unaccounted for Gas\" \u2014 repeated meter by meter.",
    "where_it_stalls": "The stall is retrospective: the gas has already flowed, often covering prior months, so this is clean-up rather than scheduling. Nearly every message carries a rework signal, and the roles are overwhelmingly requests with only one confirmation and one response visible, meaning each meter is opened as its own thread and the deal decision sits with someone outside Logistics. Identification of the right deal and counterparty is itself uncertain \u2014 in one case the contact does not recognise the deal at all (\"Daren indicated that he was not aware of this deal unless it has something to do with ENTEX\"), and in another the resolution leans on precedent from a prior year's write-off deal.",
    "why_it_recurs": "Measured meter flow and deal capture are separate records reconciled after the fact, so each accounting period surfaces a fresh set of meters whose volumes no deal covers, and every one needs an individual human decision.",
    "automation_opportunity": "A scheduled reconciliation joining measured meter volumes against active deal coverage, emitting one consolidated exception list per period \u2014 meter, days, expired or candidate deal, prior write-off history \u2014 routed to the owning commercial contact with the three standard outcomes as selectable responses, instead of one hand-written mail per meter.",
    "coherence": "tight"
  },
